IMPORT prelude

-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081 and the explorer's state key. Q's deadline is
-- anchored on P's (WITHIN 3 OF THE DEADLINE), so it is fixed in absolute
-- time (7), while P's second deadline moves with P's first act: done at 0 it
-- falls at 4, done at 4 it falls at 8. The two positions print the same
-- residual; only the second has Q's deadline pass while P's rule is still in
-- force, and `q missed` is written there and `p missed` is not.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF P, Q
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF a, b, c

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
flip MEANS
  PARTY P
  MUST a
  WITHIN 4
  HENCE
    (PARTY P
     MUST b
     WITHIN 4
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST (COMMIT `p missed` IS TRUE HENCE BREACH BY P))
    ROR
    (PARTY Q
     MUST c
     WITHIN 3 OF THE DEADLINE
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST (COMMIT `q missed` IS TRUE HENCE BREACH BY Q))
  LEST BREACH BY P

GIVEN `q missed` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      `p missed` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Q missed first` MEANS (NOT (null `q missed`)) AND (null `p missed`)

#TRACE flip AT 0 WITH
  PARTY P DOES a AT 4
  (WAITUNTIL 8)
